    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the pressure was the only thing that made me feel alive, i guess. now that it's gone, it's like there's just this huge, echoing silence. i look at my schedule for tomorrow and i just don't see any reason to bother. everything i thought mattered was just more climbing. what am i even supposed to do now that there's nowhere left to go?",
